<article class="env-lemma" id="0AVM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AVM">Lemma <span data-tag="0AVM">31.2.11</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $\varphi : \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{G}$ be a map of quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules. Assume $\mathcal{F}$ is coherent and that for every $x \in X$ one of the following happens </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}_ x \to \mathcal{G}_ x$ is an isomorphism, or 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\text{depth}(\mathcal{F}_ x) \geq 2$ and $x \not\in \text{Ass}(\mathcal{G})$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $\varphi $ is an isomorphism. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is a translation of More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0AV8" data-tag="0AV8">15.24.13</a> into the language of schemes. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>